Subject: [PATCH 5/5] =?UTF-8?q?windows-port:=20Phase=204=20follow-ups=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20scroll=20fix,=20mouse=20wheel,=20tree=20click-to-ex?=
 =?UTF-8?q?pand,=20double-click=20open?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Fix file sidebar scroll jumping the clicked row to the bottom when the
  tree exceeds the visible height; FileBrowser now tracks scroll_offset
  and only scrolls the minimum needed to keep the selection visible
- Add mouse wheel scrolling to the Files sidebar view (previously only
  SidebarView::Workspaces handled wheel events; Files/Sessions views
  shared the same hit-test rect but were never wired up)
- Add click-to-expand/collapse on the directory disclosure marker
  (previously only reachable via keyboard)
- Add double-click on a file row to open it (same as Enter)

Regression tests: update_scroll_keeps_offset_when_selection_is_already_visible,
mouse_wheel_scrolls_file_sidebar_selection, mouse_click_on_expand_marker_toggles_directory,
double_click_on_file_row_activates_it_but_a_single_click_does_not
